course: dictionary
lesson: 1175
title: A famous name from long ago
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A brontosaurus is a huge plant-eating dinosaur with a very long neck, a long tail and four thick legs. Its name means "thunder lizard", which tells you how big and heavy it must have seemed. When you meet a long word, break it into parts and ask what the parts might mean.
explain: «In 1903 Brontosaurus was judged to be the same as Apatosaurus.» Judged means decided after looking at the evidence. Then «a 2015 study said it was different enough to be its own kind again» shows that the idea changed. Scientists can change their minds when they find new evidence.
explain: Clues often hide in small words. «Old pictures put Brontosaurus in a lake, but footprints and leg bones show sauropods walked on dry land.» The word but tells you the second idea goes against the first, so the old picture must have been wrong. A sauropod is a group of big, long-necked plant-eating dinosaurs, and Brontosaurus was one of them.
fact: Brontosaurus means "thunder lizard".
fact: A brontosaurus is a noun. You can have one brontosaurus, or two brontosauruses or brontosauri.
fact: Brontosaurus was a huge plant-eating dinosaur with a very long neck, long tail and four thick legs.
fact: In 1903 scientists judged it to be the same as Apatosaurus, but a 2015 study said it was its own kind again.
fact: Science can change when new evidence is found, such as footprints and leg bones.
exercise: What does the name «Brontosaurus» tell you about the animal? | *It was huge and heavy, like thunder | It was a tiny lizard that hid under rocks | It was a bird that sang at dawn | It was a fish that lived in rivers
exercise: «In 1903 Brontosaurus was judged to be the same as Apatosaurus.» What does judged mean here? | *Decided after looking at the evidence | Lost in a game | Painted in bright colours | Shouted at loudly
exercise: «footprints and leg bones show sauropods walked on dry land» What does show mean here? | *Prove or make clear | Paint or colour | Hide from view | Break into pieces
test: What did Brontosaurus look like? | A flying reptile with big wings | A tiny dinosaur with short legs | *A huge plant-eater with a very long neck and tail | A fish with sharp teeth
test: «a 2015 study said it was different enough to be its own kind again» What does again mean here? | Forever and always | Under the water | Very quickly | *Back to how it was before
exam: «Old pictures put Brontosaurus in a lake, but footprints and leg bones show sauropods walked on dry land.» Which word shows the second idea goes against the first? | lake | pictures | *but | weight
